# swarm.config — the ONE source of truth for which Claude model the swarm worker
# (.sandcastle/main.mts) and the healer (.sandcastle/heal.sh, via model-lib.sh)
# run on (#448, learning L6). Plain KEY=value so the SAME bytes are BOTH
# sourceable by bash (model-lib.sh) and parseable by node (main.mts) — the two
# consumers can no longer drift to different hardcoded models the way
# main.mts and heal.sh silently could.
#
# Changing SWARM_MODEL here is the one-line commit that moves the whole fleet.
#
# SWARM_MODEL_MAP maps each `model-<name>` tracker label (issue #448, additive
# like `priority`) to the model id a ticket carrying that label launches on. Its
# values are the ONLY models a ticket may select — the fail-fast allowlist that
# swarm_resolve_model (model-lib.sh) enforces: an unknown selector fails LOUD
# before any worker spawns, never a silent fall back to the default. Model ids
# are Anthropic aliases, editable here without touching any consumer.
SWARM_MODEL=claude-opus-4-8
SWARM_MODEL_MAP="opus=claude-opus-4-8 sonnet=claude-sonnet-4-5 haiku=claude-haiku-4-5"
